Part (B)-II: Write Raster File 
Steps to Run Python Code in QGIS 
1.	Open QGIS. 
2.	Open your project or create a New Project. 
3.	Go to Plugins menu. 
4.	Click Python Console. 
5.	The Python Console will open at the bottom of QGIS. 
6.	In the Python Console, click the Show Editor button. 
7.	A script editor window will open. 
8.	Copy your complete Python code. 
9.	Paste the code into the script editor. 
10.	Check that the raster file path in your code is correct. 
11.	Make sure the raster file is present in that exact folder. 
12.	Click the Run Script / Green Play button. 
13.	Wait for the code to execute. 
14.	Check the Python Console output for messages. 
15.	If the raster loads successfully, it will appear in the Layers Panel. 
16.	The raster image will also appear on the Map Canvas. 
17.	If the raster has three or more bands, the RGB composite will be applied automatically. 
18.	If the raster does not appear, check the file path and run the script again. 
19.	After successful output, go to Project → Save. 
20.	Save your QGIS project. 
 
 
 
 



